`awaiting-clarification` returns only to the two statuses it can be entered from; every other status
of the run is unreachable from it, so a mis-aimed resume is refused with the reachable set — which,
through the `in-spec` superstate, also includes `cancelled`. Which of the two returns is the legal
one is `return_to`'s business and the edge's prose gate, not the manifest's.

-- fixtures/cwd/run/index.md --
---
title: "Demo"
status: awaiting-clarification
return_to: framing
---

# Demo
-- cmd --
booping transition run/index.md cross-reviewing --playbook groom
-- exit --
1
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
error: {CWD}/run/index.md (awaiting-clarification) has no edge to cross-reviewing; legal: cancelled, drafting, framing
-- expected/cwd/run/index.md --
---
title: "Demo"
status: awaiting-clarification
return_to: framing
---

# Demo
